      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Founded in 1849, Cool sprang up beside Cool Creek as miners chased the California Gold Rush.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://mohavetv.com/this-small-california-town-was-named-one-of-the-coolest-in-the-u-s-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1850 Penobscot Public House still stands as a relic of the town’s stagecoach era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cool%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before being called Cool, the area was known as Cave Valley because of limestone caves mined for lime.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Cool,_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cool sits near Auburn State Recreation Area, where whitewater rafting and canyon hikes await.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
